{"repositoryId":1204172114,"availability":"available","full":"workspace-sh/table-file-format","name":"table-file-format","description":"An open data matrix file format","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-07T18:58:26Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:57:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"develop","homepage":"https://workspace.sh/devlog","topics":[],"demo":"https://workspace-sh.github.io/table-file-format/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.964Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.964Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.964Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.964Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":[".table is an open file format for the tables people build in Airtable, Notion or a spreadsheet: typed columns, linked tables, formulas, and views such as boards and calendars.","What's different is where it lives. A .table is a file on your own disk, not a workspace on someone else's server. Inside it is plain text: a schema, and one line per row. Any tool can read it, git can track it, and you never need the app that made it to get your data back.","It is for people who work with information, not only for developers. Opened in an app, it looks and edits like the tools you already know."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/workspace-sh/table-file-format/blob/develop/README.md","fingerprint":"8665a2161ee783a61035073879772b873a20d93b242f25230e02181e2c0363fd","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:06.289Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:06.289Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":".table is an open file format for the tables people build in Airtable, Notion or a spreadsheet: typed columns, linked tables, formulas, and views such as boards and calendars.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/workspace-sh/table-file-format/blob/develop/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"8665a2161ee783a6103